<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry of the Palatinate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1487">1487</a>–<a href="/years/1552">1552</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry of the Palatinate, a Wittelsbach prince, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Utrecht from 1524 to 1529 and later of Worms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freising">Freising</a>. Unable to defend his lands against the Duke of Guelders and rebels in Utrecht, he transferred his temporal power to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in 1528. The prince-bishopric's lands became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> Lordships of Utrecht and Overijssel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-of-the-palatinate.jpg" alt="Henry of the Palatinate" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Joseph Lederer (1676-1733) and others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F%C3%BCrstengang_Bisch%C3%B6fe_48_-_Heinrich_II._von_der_Pfalz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
